class:: SpecCentroid2
summary:: Explicit spectral centroid in Hz
categories:: UGens>Analysis>MIR
related:: Guides/MIRa, Classes/SpecCentroid, Classes/SpecFlatness2, Classes/SpecPcile2

description::
Calculates the weighted mean frequency of a SuperCollider FFT frame. Bins from code::minFreq:: through code::maxFreq:: contribute either magnitude or power, and silence returns zero. The output updates when the FFT chain produces a new frame and otherwise retains that frame's result.

The implementation is a non-destructive reader of the FFT chain's spectral values. It is practically similar to link::Classes/SpecCentroid::, but makes spectrum convention, frequency limits, FFT size, units, and silence behavior explicit.

classmethods::

method:: kr

argument:: chain
An FFT chain produced with the same literal size as code::fftSize::.

argument:: minFreq
Lowest included frequency in Hz. Default 0 includes DC.

argument:: maxFreq
Highest included frequency in Hz. Zero selects Nyquist.

argument:: spectrumMode
Literal 0 weights by magnitude; 1 weights by power.

argument:: fftSize
Literal FFT size: a power of two from 256 through 8192.

returns::
Centroid frequency in Hz, or 0 for silence.

instancemethods::

examples::
The spectral centroid measures the brightness center-of-mass in Hz. In this example, it drives an adaptive spectral tilt cross-modulator: bright cymbal and snare hits open an auxiliary high-frequency pitch-shifted shimmer comb, while low-frequency bass hits remain grounded and dry. An interactive code::MIRaGUI.scope:: plots the real-time centroid frequency in Hz.
code::
(
s.waitForBoot({
    var path = MIRaGUI.soundPath("drums.wav");
    ~miraBuffer = if(path.notNil) { Buffer.read(s, path) } { nil };
    ~miraBus = Bus.control(s, 1);
    s.sync;
    ~miraExample = {
        var source = if(~miraBuffer.notNil) {
            PlayBuf.ar(1, ~miraBuffer, BufRateScale.kr(~miraBuffer), loop: 1)
        } {
            // Synthetic drum fallback
            var trig = Impulse.kr(2);
            var kick = SinOsc.ar(EnvGen.ar(Env([120, 45], [0.08], \exp), trig)) * EnvGen.ar(Env.perc(0.005, 0.3), trig);
            var snare = WhiteNoise.ar * EnvGen.ar(Env.perc(0.005, 0.15), Impulse.kr(2, 0.5));
            (kick + snare) * 0.5
        };
        // For live input instead: source = SoundIn.ar(0);

        var chain = FFT(LocalBuf(1024), source, hop: 0.5);
        var centroid = SpecCentroid2.kr(chain, fftSize: 1024);
        var brightNorm = (centroid.clip(200, 8000) / 8000).lag(0.04);
        var comb = CombC.ar(source, 0.05, (centroid.clip(200, 4000).reciprocal * 4), 0.2) * brightNorm;
        var sound = (source * 0.2) + (comb * 0.25);

        if(~miraBus.notNil) { Out.kr(~miraBus, centroid) };
        sound * Line.kr(0, 1, 0.2) ! 2
    }.play;

    ~miraGUI = MIRaGUI.scope("Spectral Centroid", ~miraBus, 0, 8000, "Hz");
});
)
::
code::
(
~miraExample.free;
if(~miraGUI.notNil) { ~miraGUI.close };
if(~miraBus.notNil) { ~miraBus.free };
if(~miraBuffer.notNil) { ~miraBuffer.free };
)
::
